{"repositoryId":881024273,"availability":"available","full":"cedricziel/signaldb","name":"signaldb","description":"A signal database for OpenTelemetry","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":6,"forks":0,"created":"2024-10-30T19:31:19Z","updated":"2026-10-13T04:22:43Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cedricziel.github.io/signaldb/","topics":["apm","logs","metrics","opentelemetry","profiles","prometheus","promql","traces"],"demo":"https://signaldb-demo.58lab.org/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:57.337Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:57.337Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:57.337Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T07:37:57.337Z","stars":6,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Observability for your homelab — one binary, one data directory.","SignalDB stores traces, logs, metrics, and continuous profiles. It ingests OpenTelemetry natively, answers Grafana's Tempo, Loki, Prometheus, and Pyroscope APIs, and ships a built-in Explore UI — so you get a full observability stack from a single process, without running four separate systems to get four signals.","It is designed to be stupidly easy to run small and able to scale out when you outgrow small: the same binary that runs on a Raspberry Pi or a NAS with SQLite and local disk splits into independent services backed by PostgreSQL and S3-compatible object storage."],"features":["One process, no dependencies. SQLite catalog, local-disk storage,","Bounded disk usage. A built-in compactor enforces 30-day retention by","A UI out of the box. Logs, traces, and metrics are explorable at","Runs on your hardware. Multi-arch images (amd64/arm64) built on"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cedricziel/signaldb/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f6a2f3e91eb149f2d2b860b6f74eebc3b063313506742e4d32d9bdea985a0e3c","extractedAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:57.464Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:57.464Z","pro